{"availability":"available","full":"kingkillery/Spreadsheet_LLM_Encoder","name":"Spreadsheet_LLM_Encoder","description":"Encodes Xcel Spreadsheets into Spreadsheet LLM Encoded JSON (Easier for LLM's to Understand)","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":25,"forks":7,"created":"2025-03-15T04:19:35Z","updated":"2026-08-06T03:00:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://spreadsheetllmencoder.streamlit.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T13:36:10.766Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T13:36:10.766Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T13:36:10.766Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T13:36:10.766Z","stars":25,"forks":7}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This repository contains a paper-inspired implementation of the SpreadsheetLLM encoding method introduced by Microsoft Research in July 2024. It implements several paper-facing prompt surfaces and compression mechanics, but it should not be treated as a reproduction of the paper's reported metrics unless matching datasets, splits, model procedures, and baselines are supplied.","SpreadsheetLLM is a novel approach to encoding spreadsheets that addresses the limitations of traditional methods when working with LLMs. Instead of converting spreadsheets into simple tables or flattened structures, this method:","This approach significantly improves an LLM's ability to understand, reason about, and manipulate spreadsheet data."],"features":["Preserves structural relationships between cells using anchor points","Maintains formatting information for better visual understanding","Creates compact representations through inverted indexing","Handles merged cells and complex layouts effectively"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kingkillery/Spreadsheet_LLM_Encoder/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ff8c92af281dc1f54f098455605ac9d71d2a25861e3529377eb1f151f781c2cb","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T13:36:10.914Z"},"overviewChec